{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman","id":198991,"title":"Thor is now a woman","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-16T08:52:31-07:00","id":198991,"title":"Thor is now a woman","content":"<a href=\"http://io9.com/marvels-new-thor-is-a-woman-1605307213\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/marvels-new-thor-is-a-woman-1605307213</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Thor is no longer worthy of holding the hammer and is being replaced by a woman? Interesting...<br /> <br /> Now, admittedly I'm not an avid comic book reader, nor do I read Marvel Comics at all, but at the same time I can't help but wonder at the thought process of this. Not because they've changed the character identity to a female, but by how they're setting it up. <br /> <br /> I mean, it'd be one thing for Thor to have died and a woman take his place (which I think would make more sense) but Thor becomes permanently unworthy so another person has to take his place? Isn't that kind of insulting to the people who like the character of Thor? <br /> <br /> I mean isn't this like if writers took Batman and said 'Batman finally lost his self-control and killed a thug in cold blood, now another person has to take up the mantle of the bat permanently'...<br /> <br /> Thoughts on this whole situation?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:06:49-07:00","id":199009,"title":"","content":"Eh, &quot;Thor screws up, loses Mjolnir, someone else carries his mantle until he gets his head on straight/proves himself worthy once more&quot; has been done before. This is a lot closer to Knightfall than it is to the scenario you posit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:26:46-07:00","id":199032,"title":"","content":"There was a &quot;What if&quot; issue that did this earlier with Jane Foster finding the hammer:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img4.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20100816122241/marveldatabase/images/thumb/9/93/What_If%3F_Vol_1_10.jpg/200px-What_If%3F_Vol_1_10.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:32:07-07:00","id":199037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=199009#post199009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, &quot;Thor screws up, loses Mjolnir, someone else carries his mantle until he gets his head on straight/proves himself worthy once more&quot; has been done before. This is a lot closer to Knightfall than it is to the scenario you posit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>the interviews indicate Thor isn't going to be proving he's worthy again. This new woman is Thor from here on out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:37:31-07:00","id":199038,"title":"","content":"I predict this fails miserably. Just more writers screwing things up for the sake of shock in the hopes of provoking sales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:38:02-07:00","id":199039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman#post198991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean isn't this like if writers took Batman and said 'Batman finally lost his self-control and killed a thug in cold blood, now another person has to take up the mantle of the bat permanently'...</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't they done that before? Multiple times? I feel like that's part and parcel of the whole comic book genre. Of course this isn't a permanent move. If it's popular enough, they'll reboot the character in a new series of comics eventually with a slightly tweaked origin story. I'm interested to see this new Thor. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:43:58-07:00","id":199045,"title":"","content":"I think we could sit here for a few months detailing all the times Marvel alone has made such a statement and gone back on it eventually.<br /> <br /> Soon or later they'll go back to male Thor. Because comics.<br /> <br /> If this female Thor proves popular enough, she'll join the ranks of Marvel characters that are former Thors that still have power (Beta Ray Bill and Thunderstrike) and good not-so-old Thor Girl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T09:59:26-07:00","id":199069,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I have less objection to the idea of Thor falling and being replaced (gender of the new one is a non-issue) than I do to the fact that they're treating Thor as a title. The number of beings that can wield </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Mj\u00f6lnir can be tallied on one hand, Thor is *not* short hand for &quot;the person that wields Mj\u00f6lnir&quot; it's the proper name of someone. It's saying &quot;not only is this character replaceable, we can take their name because they're that interchangeable&quot;<br /> <br /> if Batman retired and another took his place (which has happened in some tellings) the new one doesn't go by Bruce Wayne.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:00:57-07:00","id":199074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=199037#post199037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the interviews indicate Thor isn't going to be proving he's worthy again. This new woman is Thor from here on out...</div> </div> </div> </div>The writer says he wanted to do a story &quot;about somebody else wielding the hammer for a while.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I'm reading out of all this is that nobody on board actually expect this to last forever, that this Thor will displace her predecessor in hearts and minds and stick it out for the ages. On the other hand, nobody on board has a specific, limited story arc in mind. They'll do this for a while--probably a years or two--before they figure she's built enough heat on her own and it's time for Thor Odinson to wield Mjolnir again.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:01:54-07:00","id":199075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=199037#post199037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interviews indicate Thor isn't going to be proving he's worthy again. This new woman is Thor from here on out...</div> </div> </div> </div>The interviews indicated Superman wouldn't return from the dead, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:02:24-07:00","id":199078,"title":"","content":"Marvel is cyclical. Most comics are, but Marvel is especially horrid about it. Every time they have had a major plotline that is supposed to &quot;shake the foundations of the Marvel Universe&quot; then things have been changed back to normal within a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:20:50-07:00","id":199096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=199069#post199069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I have less objection to the idea of Thor falling and being replaced (gender of the new one is a non-issue) than I do to the fact that they're treating Thor as a title. The number of beings that can wield </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Mj\u00f6lnir can be tallied on one hand, Thor is *not* short hand for &quot;the person that wields Mj\u00f6lnir&quot; it's the proper name of someone. It's saying &quot;not only is this character replaceable, we can take their name because they're that interchangeable&quot;<br /> <br /> if Batman retired and another took his place (which has happened in some tellings) the new one doesn't go by Bruce Wayne.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I initially had the same reaction, but as long as the original Thor doesn't lose his actual name, I don't think there is much of a problem in other people using it as a heroic codename due to the established legacy. I mean, did you also complain when Eric Masterson went by Thor? Or when Beta Ray Bill went by Beta Ray Thor?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Anyone else a bit disappointed with her costume? It is not horrible or anything, but a bit over-designed for my taste. Well, Thor's costume design also got quite a bit busier over time, so I guess it was to be expected, but his larger body mass allows all those details to look more spread out. Also, I think it would look better with a larger plate or mail armor covering her torso above the big belt. <br /> <br /> <br /> also, I found this amusing<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.kinja-img.com/gawker-media/image/upload/s--5sf_VraX--/c_fit,fl_progressive,q_80,w_320/ossp3cv8aiehnocvnxil.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.kinja-img.com/gawker-media/image/upload/s--Zc9oCjop--/c_fit,fl_progressive,q_80,w_320/asyr5zynaenfvxvr4o7g.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 07-16-2014, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T10:29:21-07:00","id":199100,"title":"","content":"Thor is just dressing as a woman so he can go to a wedding with Loki and get his hammer back from the giants. At least that's what I remember happening in Norse myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T11:09:46-07:00","id":199125,"title":"","content":"I actually rather like the costume and design. It's kind of cool(if still prone to the failings of comic book logic on armor).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:17:02-07:00","id":199193,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Whosoever holds this hammer, if he be worthy, shall possess the power of Thor.&quot;[</i> I would definitely say that the word to focus on should be &quot;worthy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:42:03-07:00","id":199216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=199069#post199069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have less objection to the idea of Thor falling and being replaced (gender of the new one is a non-issue) than I do to the fact that they're treating Thor as a title</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't make any sense to the Norse mythology, but it works just fine within the Marvel canon (as much as anything can in that convoluted mess).<br /> <br /> The comics do have a separation of the physical being and the divine essence that they embody, allowing for those divine essences to be transferred from one physical vessel to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T14:18:10-07:00","id":199238,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the original idea of the character being that he was a regular man who transformed into Thor (later retconned into a false memory placed over actual Thor)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T15:58:06-07:00","id":199361,"title":"","content":"Basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:20:00-07:00","id":200084,"title":"","content":"I pretty much covered why I don't like this in the comic thread. I have nothing against &quot;female&quot; superheroes(that is vs half naked women written just for guys) and I'm not a big Thor fan. I think the situation is bull shit for a lot of reasons. Even more so in this situation when they could be playing up Thor Girl. Maybe they will prove me wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T09:48:17-07:00","id":200124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=200084#post200084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more so in this situation when they could be playing up Thor Girl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without any actual practical knowledge of marketing or anything like that, here's what I'm suspecting the rationale is:<br /> <br /> If you create a female Thor-alike in her own title while Thor has his own, you're going to have some people who pick it up, absolutely. Primarily, you'll have the folks who would buy anything with a Thor logo on it, and you'll probably have some people wanting to support a female superhero.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you replace Thor Odinson with a female Thor...well, yes, you're <i>absolutely</i> going to hemorrhage some readers who will be upset. With luck, good writing, and word-of-mouth, you can win most of them back. Meanwhile, you probably keep the majority of the audience of Thor as it was, and add the people wanting to support the female superhero, as above.<br /> <br /> So the Thor completists and whatever miscellaneous audience won't be shelling out more money, but at the same time you're not having to pay the costs to write and illustrate a whole other series.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, you're building heat for this new character. When--not if, when--she ceases to be Thor and the Odinson takes his hammer back, assuming you did your job right, you have a pretty good idea of whether it's financial sense to spin her off into her own book, and can keep the new readership you gained from this storyline while you're at it..<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, by making this character the main star of an existing comic, you're simultaneously attacking a second barrier that going straight to spinoff would run headlong into: the idea that this is &quot;<span style=\"color:#EE82EE\">Thor for Girls.</span>&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 07-17-2014, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:05:16-07:00","id":200162,"title":"","content":"This new Thor looks cool. <br /> <br /> That said, the idea that whoever holds Mjolinar is Thor is kinda dumb. We've had other people wield Mjolinar in the past and that wasn't the case. <br /> <br /> Whatever though, I don't follow Marvel comics anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:24:38-07:00","id":200209,"title":"","content":"As I alluded in the comic-book thread, Thor is kind of a package deal. Changing the package will be a deal breaker for many who are familiar with the machismo that was part of that package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T11:59:41-07:00","id":200319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=200124#post200124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without any actual practical knowledge of marketing or anything like that, here's what I'm suspecting the rationale is:<br /> <br /> If you create a female Thor-alike in her own title while Thor has his own, you're going to have some people who pick it up, absolutely. Primarily, you'll have the folks who would buy anything with a Thor logo on it, and you'll probably have some people wanting to support a female superhero.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you replace Thor Odinson with a female Thor...well, yes, you're <i>absolutely</i> going to hemorrhage some readers who will be upset. With luck, good writing, and word-of-mouth, you can win most of them back. Meanwhile, you probably keep the majority of the audience of Thor as it was, and add the people wanting to support the female superhero, as above.<br /> <br /> So the Thor completists and whatever miscellaneous audience won't be shelling out more money, but at the same time you're not having to pay the costs to write and illustrate a whole other series.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, you're building heat for this new character. When--not if, when--she ceases to be Thor and the Odinson takes his hammer back, assuming you did your job right, you have a pretty good idea of whether it's financial sense to spin her off into her own book, and can keep the new readership you gained from this storyline while you're at it..<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, by making this character the main star of an existing comic, you're simultaneously attacking a second barrier that going straight to spinoff would run headlong into: the idea that this is &quot;<span style=\"color:#EE82EE\">Thor for Girls.</span>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's whey I think they are shooting themselves in the foot. There are plans for at least two more Avengers(2&amp;3) with the same actors. If it attracts new people they are going to hit an extreme brick wall of &quot;Wait Thor is female&quot;? People might buy it in spite of that, but unless they do some heavy advertising(heavier than what is likely to be another block buster movie or two) you are not going to have near as many people coming to it because Thor is female.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=200209#post200209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I alluded in the comic-book thread, Thor is kind of a package deal. Changing the package will be a deal breaker for many who are familiar with the machismo that was part of that package.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way you put that, because I don't think that male/female fan or the particulars of why matter and are beside the point. This character, as it is, is why they are currently coming to read it. A female Thor totally changes that dynamic. At a time when everything else is going to be pointing toward a male Thor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 07-17-2014, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T23:48:20-07:00","id":201854,"title":"","content":"My only question is why not start with a fresh character and build from there? I don't see the problem of having a <i>Valkyrja</i> like Brynhildr, Skuld or even Freyja pick up a longsword, a Dane axe or even a hammer and fighting to protect Earth alongside Thor Odinsson. Marvel has the resources to pour into a new character and title and to build it up. It seems absurd to take a legacy character who is currently part of their Phase 02 movie franchise and change it. Why not introduce the new comic character alongside Thor in Phase 03?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","name":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T06:42:47-07:00","id":202054,"title":"","content":"Well, a few things come t mind:<br /> <br /> 1) The Thor franchise already has most of those characters in use at some point (and it is heavily implied one of them is going to be the new Thor as it is). Pulling a &quot;new&quot; character from the same well as Thor in the 616 Marvel-verse is pretty much impossible at this point. There are going to be legacy/continuity holdovers regardless.<br /> <br /> 2) This is pretty standard comic book industry stuff. Legacy character comic titles are generally where new characters and retooled characters get introduced before they get spun off into their own thing if they do well, or just get added to the title's existing cast of support characters.<br /> <br /> 3) Marvel has done pretty well by not worrying about the comics and movies not lining up. This is hardly the first time there's been a major character thing happen in the comics that didn't mesh well at all with the movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T07:05:50-07:00","id":202075,"title":"","content":"The Marvel Cinematic Universe as opposed to the Marvel Comics...which is further differentiated by the productions that own which titles. (Sony, Disney, Fox)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T07:43:23-07:00","id":202123,"title":"","content":"So there was something I ran across on twitter last night that I hadn't realized until now... and it's relevant.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#292F33\"><span style=\"font-family:Gotham Narrow SSm\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Disney owns marvel. Marvel owns Thor. Thor is the son of a king. Thor is now female. Thor is now a Disney princess.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T08:17:44-07:00","id":202144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=202123#post202123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there was something I ran across on twitter last night that I hadn't realized until now... and it's relevant.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#292F33\"><span style=\"font-family:Gotham Narrow SSm\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Disney owns marvel. Marvel owns Thor. Thor is the son of a king. Thor is now female. Thor is now a Disney princess.&quot;</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Disney's just leaping forward by steps and bounds now,aren't they?<br /> <br /> *now hears Chris Hemsworth singing Let It Go*<br /> <br /> *Is strangely okay with this