--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somebody punch me in the ovaries! I need to feel MANLY!</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&amp;v=CfIKRQ4sTfU\" data-code=\"CfIKRQ4sTfU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/CfIKRQ4sTfU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T12:12:29-07:00","id":203126,"title":"","content":"Eh, marvel Thor already had precious little to do with the \u00c5s from our myths as it was. Change the gender, make him a space alien, who gives a rat's arse anymore ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T19:49:47-07:00","id":203396,"title":"","content":"The Marvel Cinematic Universe did screw things up. And now the comic-books are going one better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:21:07-07:00","id":203415,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how either of those statements work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:36:10-07:00","id":203423,"title":"","content":"Thor was never a space alien in the comic books. If Thor translated to the big screen how he is in the comic books he would have ripped off Starks armor and told him that Asgardian armor is better.<br /> The comic book Thor that is now a woman is either going to lose that machismo, or we're going to see just how feminist things can go before a return to &quot;normal&quot; either in time for the Avengers 2, or things will take a dive faster than they thought and will have to fix things well before the movie. Either way, this will be temporary no matter what they say. After all, most of the sales are from the male half of the species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:11:46-07:00","id":203507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203423#post203423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, most of the sales are from the male half of the species.</div> </div> </div> </div>And... that's supposed to encourage them to turn Thor back into a hunky man instead of a sexy woman... how exactly?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:19:42-07:00","id":203513,"title":"","content":"I can't speak for the comic books. I am not that Lorax.<br /> <br /> But in regards to the movies....sooooo what?<br /> <br /> I mean, purist &quot;That's not like the comic book&quot; ranting aside that should have died ages ago(because seriously, if you're going to be disappointed by degrees of faithlessness, you should have stopped watching most blockbusters about six or seven years ago), the Thor movies have been decent(albeit not great), it feels much more organic to pseudo-science hypertech of the entire Cinematic Universe, and thus has greater consistency with itself, and interaction between Thor and Tony-and Thor and everyone else-has felt very true to character and circumstance.<br /> <br /> If you're on some rant about the comic books and their relation to the movies, I can't help you. I think the way most mainstream American comics work are silly anyways. But as far as the movies go, which should be judged by their own merits-not the least of which because movies are very different medium of storytelling compared to comics that appeal to a different audience-your complaints have about as much impact as a fart on a really windy plain.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203507#post203507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And... that's supposed to encourage them to turn Thor back into a hunky man instead of a sexy woman... how exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously. I actually briefly considered buying the Thor comic once people started talking about a female Thor. The armor(not perfect) did a lot to help that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-21-2014, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:20:22-07:00","id":203588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203423#post203423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thor was never a space alien in the comic books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The MCU doing things differently than the comics is not the same thing as screwing them up.<br /> <br /> And there was that whole Beta Ray &quot;I'm a space alien!&quot; Bill saga where he wielded Thor's power for a bit and all that. And that time Thor was a frog. And all the AU takes on Thor (esp. Ultimate since the MCU is heavily a mixture of 616 and Ultimate stuff).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Thor translated to the big screen how he is in the comic books he would have ripped off Starks armor and told him that Asgardian armor is better. </div> </div> </div>Odd... why does he never do this again? Oh, right, because that's stupid. Thor has tons of bravado. And there's no reason a female Thor character can't have bravado either. Calling it machismo is just an attempt to claim there's something thing inherently gendered about his attitude (something that the comics don't support with the warrior inclined Asgaridan women).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either way, this will be temporary no matter what they say. After all, most of the sales are from the male half of the species. </div> </div> </div>It has nothing to do with the gender of the readers. Plenty of female lead characters have shown that male readers don't want male-only leads.<br /> <br /> This always happens with comics because comics always return to the status quo. This has been covered more than adequately","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:28:28-07:00","id":203590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203588#post203588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Heavy Arms being a general stud*</div> </div> </div> </div>I would send you cookies if it didn't cost an arm and a leg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T06:35:13-07:00","id":203774,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n203588]We've already seen how low grade Thor is on screen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203588#post203588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd... why does he never do this again? Oh, right, because that's stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Again?&quot;<br /> When did Thor do this on screen before? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203588#post203588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thor has tons of bravado. And there's no reason a female Thor character can't have bravado either. Calling it machismo is just an attempt to claim there's something thing inherently gendered about his attitude (something that the comics don't support with the warrior inclined Asgaridan women).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thor has history, mythology, legend...the whole package deal.<br /> And now they want to change that whole package and base that into a girl?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203588#post203588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has nothing to do with the gender of the readers. Plenty of female lead characters have shown that male readers don't want male-only leads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing to do with that. But everything to do with changing an existing character that already has an established fanbase.<br /> They should make a new character lead. Don't change the old established material for the sake of shock value or for being trendy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203588#post203588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This always happens with comics because comics always return to the status quo. This has been covered more than adequately</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that &quot;status quo&quot; has the customer base covered. And they don't want to lose it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:15:40-07:00","id":203821,"title":"","content":"Shadow, are you not familiar with turns of phrase?<br /> <br /> The use of &quot;again&quot; doesn't mean he's done it before, it's to assert that the answer to the question was either already discussed or is common knowledge.<br /> <br /> As for everything else, I let other people hash it out, but I would like to point out that it seems silly to be all worked up over something you know is going to be a phase. This too shall pass, so even if you don't like it, why worry over it?<br /> <br /> The established fanbase isn't going anywhere, they know the score(I feel dirty saying that, but the comic book industry has more right to quote Michael Bay on that then anyone else), and the stunt might actually draw some people-hell, it almost did with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T09:40:08-07:00","id":203916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203774#post203774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've already seen how low grade Thor is on screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your opinion. Some people have liked the MCU Thor, other people have not. All three of the MCU movies with Thor have &quot;fresh&quot; ratings on Rotten Tomatoes even if the Thor movies are not the best of the MCU. So it seems fair to say that MCU Thor is not the best of the bunch, but that doesn't mean he's bad.<br /> <br /> Which is actually fairly consistent with his presence in the comics. Thor is a solid mainstay of Marvel's lineup, but consistently not been the big seller with his solo titles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When did Thor do this on screen before? </div> </div> </div>My point was when did he do that in the comics as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Comics Thor, for the most part, does not run around ripping into human's for their lesser tech/magic. The whole point of his Marvel origin story is that he had to learn to be more respectful and humble; even with &quot;lesser&quot; beings like humans. The whole &quot;being worthy&quot; thing that's always been central to his Marvel mythos. Walking up to Tony and ruining one of the Iron Man suits for the lulz is not a Thor worthy action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thor has history, mythology, legend...the whole package deal.<br /> And now they want to change that whole package and base that into a girl? </div> </div> </div>Why is there an assumption that any of the package is lost just because Thor is going to be a woman?<br /> <br /> Keep using words like machismo and girl all you want, but little semantic games don't actually demonstrate the point at hand. This is far from the first time the mantle of the Thor has not rested on the biological son of Odin. If anything, it is part of comic Thor's history, mythology, legend, and whole package that other people are capable of taking up the name and power of Thor when Odinson isn't up to the job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing to do with that. </div> </div> </div>Then why did you bring up the gender of the majority of comic book purchasers? You explicitly brought up comic book fans gender as one of the reasons Thor should not be changed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But everything to do with changing an existing character that already has an established fanbase.<br /> They should make a new character lead. Don't change the old established material for the sake of shock value or for being trendy. </div> </div> </div>Comic books do this all the time. If this drove away fans in significant numbers Marvel and DC would be broke and belly up by now.<br /> <br /> Comics do this all the time precisely because it works. Call the marketing and creative strategies that lead to these sorts of changes and their inevitable reversion back to the status quo by whatever terms you want. It doesn't matter. If it didn't end up making comic book companies money, they wouldn't be doing it. If shocking changes sells, shock is going to happen. If trendiness sells, trendy things will happen. Because that's what Marvel does, sell comic books.<br /> <br /> If part of this leads to their being more diversity on the covers of comic books, I don't see how that's not a positive side effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:06:33-07:00","id":203930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203916#post203916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's your opinion. Some people have liked the MCU Thor, other people have not. All three of the MCU movies with Thor have &quot;fresh&quot; ratings on Rotten Tomatoes even if the Thor movies are not the best of the MCU.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because we enjoy the movies for what they are. But no one considers that the comic-book Thor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203916#post203916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is there an assumption that any of the package is lost just because Thor is going to be a woman?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you missed the &quot;history&quot; part? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203916#post203916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep using words like machismo and girl all you want, but little semantic games don't actually demonstrate the point at hand. This is far from the first time the mantle of the Thor has not rested on the biological son of Odin. If anything, it is part of comic Thor's history, mythology, legend, and whole package that other people are capable of taking up the name and power of Thor when Odinson isn't up to the job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one appreciate the differences in gender as well as respect the history that comes with the whole package. This is the same reason why I have no problem with Sam Wilson as Cap.<br /> <br /> I give this a few months, 6 tops before they re-spin everything.<br /> <br /> Distraction alert...Hot <a href=\"http://ricochet.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/thora1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Thor chick</a> Sign her up!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:47:06-07:00","id":203958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203774#post203774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thor has history, mythology, legend...the whole package deal. And now they want to change that whole package and base that into a girl?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what &quot;change that whole package&quot; means (though I am immature enough to be making &quot;package&quot; puns in my head), because I don't know which mythology you're referring to; Norse, Marvel, Marvel 616, or what. Would you please clarify?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203774#post203774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should make a new character lead.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. She's getting a book and everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203774#post203774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't change the old established material for the sake of shock value or for being trendy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not. Nothing about Thor's established material--which by definition means his past--is being changed. Only his future is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T11:46:39-07:00","id":204031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203930#post203930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, because we enjoy the movies for what they are. But no one considers that the comic-book Thor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... and?<br /> <br /> I'm lost at to what your point is on this part of the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe you missed the &quot;history&quot; part? </div> </div> </div>Nope. Relevant parts of comic Thor's history:<br /> <br /> 1) Thor's power can be separated from Thor Odison and given to another who is Thor until Odinson gets his shit together (if at all depending which continuity we're talking about).<br /> <br /> 2) Thor's supporting mythos includes women with equal bravado as Thor.<br /> <br /> 3) Everything that is currently canon in Thor's history is remaining so (as flimsy as comic canon is).<br /> <br /> So yeah. Just saying, &quot;but what about the history!&quot; doesn't work. Thor's history completely supports this direction as being viable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I for one appreciate the differences in gender as well as respect the history that comes with the whole package. </div> </div> </div>You've yet to give a single reason why differences between the genders matters to this case. Especially the comic's canon views of gender in Asgard, which does not support being a powerful warrior deity as something regulated to a specific gender (Sif, Brunnhilde and the Valkyrior). Lack of a gendered view on who is allowed to be a warrior is part of the history and whole package you're talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the same reason why I have no problem with Sam Wilson as Cap. </div> </div> </div>So... gender changes ruin things, but racial changes are cool? You don't see anything wrong with consistency with these arguments?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I give this a few months, 6 tops before they re-spin everything. </div> </div> </div>I think it'll last a bit longer than that myself, but it depends on how things go, and what they do with Odinson while someone else has the hammer and powers. But you'll notice that there's little argument over things eventually going back to the status quo. I'm not even sure what the point of bringing it up is any more.<br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=203958#post203958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(though I am immature enough to be making &quot;package&quot; puns in my head)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T12:05:37-07:00","id":204039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=202890#post202890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=200124#post200124\">Here is a theory.</a> I have no way of knowing if it's true, but it makes sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. Total speculation on my part, FWIW. I have no special insight into the market at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=202991#post202991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh Jim, Mockery will get you <i>everywhere</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>&gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Wait, I'm a chauffeur now?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 07-21-2014, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","