:"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-21-2014, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T16:20:43-07:00","id":204334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=204306#post204306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's your opinion. When this shit sandwich doesn't sell, they'll get rid of her soon enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I've provided evidence to back up why I feel my opinion has merit beyond personal preference. You haven't.<br /> <br /> As well... how do you know this is going to be a &quot;shit sandwich&quot; that isn't going to sell? It hasn't even come out yet for anyone to read to say how good or bad it is. It hasn't had anytime to play out a few issues to see if it'll be a good arc that keeps the core fans happy and possibly attract other readers. What's your basis for this assertion?<br /> <br /> And yeah, if you haven't noticed? <b>We all agree</b> that male Thor will be back. Because the big comic companies very rarely allow major characters to have this sort of change for long. Even characters that easily allow for multiple people to hold the mantle (ex: Batman) go back to the status quo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=204316#post204316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is that, anyways? Her face seems familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>If my Google-fu is working, the face is Amber Heard with some digital work to blend her into Thor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T16:23:54-07:00","id":204337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=204334#post204334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well... how do you know this is going to be a &quot;shit sandwich&quot; that isn't going to sell? It hasn't even come out yet for anyone to read to say how good or bad it is. It hasn't had anytime to play out a few issues to see if it'll be a good arc that keeps the core fans happy and possibly attract other readers. What's your basis for this assertion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-misunderstood misogyny, would be my guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T17:06:46-07:00","id":204370,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, I'm still waiting for my lesbian Jahve superhero and her gay sidekick Jesus. When is Marvel going to supply this ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T17:11:39-07:00","id":204375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=204306#post204306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's your opinion. When this shit sandwich doesn't sell, they'll get rid of her soon enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Scuse me? I think that this is an interesting new direction for Marvel to go with this comic. I will probably subscribe for a bit to see how I like it, and I never would have considered subscribing to normal Thor.<br /> <br /> Unbacked assertions are unbacked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T17:12:01-07:00","id":204376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=204312#post204312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> K, I'm good with the change now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, that'd work...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T19:18:48-07:00","id":204529,"title":"","content":"I'm enjoying the sarcasm I'm reading <a href=\"http://blog.sarcasmsociety.com/entertainment/thor-to-be-a-female-superhero-in-new-incarnation.html\" target=\"_blank\">elsewhere</a><br /> <i><br /> This is a pretty clever way to help young girls feel empowered\u2014why create a new female superhero or resurrect one from ancient mythology when you can just make a popular superhero a female. It sends the perfect message to little girls everywhere: the only way to be a strong woman is to take on the abilities, powers, and name of a man. </i><br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> Maybe DC will come around and make Wonder Woman a man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T19:54:02-07:00","id":204569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=204529#post204529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm enjoying the sarcasm I'm reading <a href=\"http://blog.sarcasmsociety.com/entertainment/thor-to-be-a-female-superhero-in-new-incarnation.html\" target=\"_blank\">elsewhere</a><br /> <i><br /> This is a pretty clever way to help young girls feel empowered\u2014why create a new female superhero or resurrect one from ancient mythology when you can just make a popular superhero a female. It sends the perfect message to little girls everywhere: the only way to be a strong woman is to take on the abilities, powers, and name of a man. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's cute and everything, but I can't help thinking it's deliberately missing the point of how difficult it is to establish a new character in the existing big comic universes without piggybacking that character off an existing one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T20:09:06-07:00","id":204579,"title":"","content":"Hmf...<a href=\"http://forums.superherohype.com/showthread.php?t=482907\" target=\"_blank\">Superhero Hype</a> is pretty condemning. As one poster puts it; <i>Dude, we all know it's temporary. That's the problem. They do stuff like this yearly now. It's played the f**k out.</i> ...now...this I think would have been acceptable since it's temporary anyway: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://31.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m5o3wyQG9B1rxyld0o1_1280.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T22:49:25-07:00","id":204687,"title":"","content":"Huh. While I wouldn't have said that I saw this coming, after seeing how mutable the Asgardians were in JMS' run of Thor and especially having seen the identity crisis Loki went through, the idea that &quot;Thor&quot; is as much mantle as it is an identity seems like an intriguing way to go.<br /> <br /> I'm not in a position to pick up subs right now, but if the writing turns out good I might pick up in trade form on Comixology.<br /> <br /> As to why not Thor Girl...that's a whole different can of worms they would have had to tackle before putting out the book. Haven't paid attention to Thor's side of the universe for a while so I don't know what's going on with Valkyrie either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 07-22-2014, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T01:12:43-07:00","id":204783,"title":"","content":"Just want to point out, the Brony market demonstrates that there's a fairly sizeable audience of, predominantly but not entirely, males out there quite happy to spend great quantities of disposable income on things aimed at girls and women.<br /> <br /> Hell the last comic I bought (as in, the only comics I have ever bought in my entire life) is the MLP series. I am now eyeing up a Dr. Strange one on Comixology because he's a wizard and apparently appeared as a recommended character if you like Twilight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also also. The majority of the comic book buying audience is male. Ok. Why not try and find a way of getting the other 50% of the world's population on board with your product? If their marketing and consumer research departments believe that using an existing charcater and doing a gender swap is an effective way forward then let them try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T06:42:31-07:00","id":204905,"title":"","content":"51%, actually. There are slightly fewer men in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T06:53:38-07:00","id":204906,"title":"","content":"Despite China's best efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:59:31-07:00","id":205008,"title":"","content":"The global human sex ratio (at least according to the CIA Worldbook and Wolfram Alpha, I haven't looked at a lot of places) seems to have ticked back in the other direction; with males hitting ~50.3% last year. And while blaming China is fun (and they are part of the reason why that flipped), India is more to blame for this because there is equal artificial sex selection at birth, while India has a much larger birth rate and a slightly smaller gap in the life expectancy of males vs. female.<br /> <br /> Though I'm pretty sure the global numbers aren't that important to Marvel's strategies, and even then the global numbers include lots of people that are not considered prime targets.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of this really matters to the more important point that trying to get females of multiple age brackets into comics is all pluses for the comic book industry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T18:31:09-07:00","id":205513,"title":"","content":"Oh, I like <a href=\"https://this guy&#39;s design\" target=\"_blank\">this guy's design</a> for Thor not-Odinsson much better than the official one<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s28.postimg.org/j4lhqzbql/the_mighty_thor_by_danielmurrayart_d7rijnf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Meanwhile, back in the actual comics, it seems Thor Odinson will be<a href=\"http://io9.com/heres-what-thor-will-look-like-now-that-hes-no-longer-t-1609140391\" target=\"_blank\"> cosplaying as Tetsuo from Akira</a>:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s27.postimg.org/vtkin3ggj/kn2bvrasw5lqyl8j9hvy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s27.postimg.org/59rxkyfwz/gsyu1jwafppxji1glnma.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T04:19:56-07:00","id":262762,"title":"","content":"I dislike this quite a lot. Thor becomes a woman, Wolverine dies, Falcon retires and becomes Captain America, seriously? Marvel completely ran out of ideas and started screwing up everything so just they can sell more comic books even if it's just for all fans to by and &quot;see how it turns out, maybe it's good&quot;?<br /> <br /> 1st - It's not the woman superhero that bothers me, but the substitution of Thor. As fellow roleplayers and probably, a lot are fans of Scion, something that isn't lacking is amazing female goddesses that could enter the Marvel Universe and kick ass! Revamping Thor is not, in my opinion the way to go.<br /> <br /> 2nd - Wolverine dies? Yeah like Jean Grey died, like Cyclops died and bunch of others.<br /> <br /> 3rd - Let's get rid of Falcon because he isn't popular enough and make him Captain American to show the world we are culturally diverse and in touch with the modern times! -.-'<br /> <br /> I used to be a huge Marvel fanboy, but now I hate it. They're just recycling ideas and concepts trying to look political correct and modern! Superheroes exist, they have their identities, stories and backgrounds. Keep it that way, don't change it. If Marvel wants more women, gays, different races, etc. build new and interesting superheroes/villains! I'm all up for that and support it 100%. But could it not mess with around with our childhood heroes? DC wanted a Batgirl they did a Batgirl, they didn't replace Batman!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T04:50:58-07:00","id":262771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=262762#post262762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolverine dies? Yeah like Jean Grey died, like Cyclops died and bunch of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I've been hearing from a lot of sources is yes, of course Wolverine will <i>eventually</i> return--this is comics, after all--but Marvel and Disney are going to keep him dead as a way of combating Fox, which apparently has some kind of licensing rights with all the X-characters and gets a piece of the pie on all X-merchandise. They're killing Wolverine and paring down the mutant universe to try to starve Fox out and force them to drop the movie and licensing rights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=262762#post262762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's get rid of Falcon because he isn't popular enough and make him Captain American to show the world we are culturally diverse and in touch with the modern times!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible this is true, I suppose, but if you have some actual proof that's their motivation rather than just a desire to tell a generational story of a mantle surviving the man who originally carried it, then I would like to see that proof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=262762#post262762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Marvel wants more women, gays, different races, etc. build new and interesting superheroes/villains! I'm all up for that and support it 100%.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone, I think someone on this forum site, pointed out, that is a big financial risk. By making an event out of the change, Marvel attracts new readers who might get hooked and probably keeps more old readers on the current title than they lose to outrage; that built-in audience will serve as a basis for predicting whether the character's eventual ongoing book will be profitable to make. I don't know what the problem is with shaking up the status quo anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 09-22-2014, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T05:20:20-07:00","id":262776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=262771#post262771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible this is true, I suppose, but if you have some actual proof that's their motivation rather than just a desire to tell a generational story of a mantle surviving the man who originally carried it, then I would like to see that proof.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proof isn't relevant to selling an idea. They want us to believe so people will buy more comic books...don't need proof of this. It's just business.<br /> Had it been any other character this would have been too tough to sell. But it's Sam Wilson. I could buy that for a while.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T07:23:13-07:00","id":262835,"title":"","content":"If I there was any proof of anything then it would be official reason, what I wrote is what I think is really behind all these changes. And you've seen it in the movies. Samuel L. Jackson as Nick Fury? Really?!? The resemblance is uncanny! And I gave Kingpin for free since I can't see any other actor do him better than Michael Clark Duncan (he had the perfect physical traits and I love his role, well the only thing I liked about that movie anyway lol). Now the new movie of the Fantastic Four will also be featuring a black Johnny Storm / Human Torch. I can't see any reason for Marvel to be turning every damn character black! If they want racial diversity do a movie based on Bishop, he is one of the most badass and interesting characters in the X-Men and Marvel Universe! With huge potential for stories and moral dilemmas! As the comics go, even if Sam Wilson is getting old and a new Captain is needed, why do they have to get rid of Falcon and not just come up with a successor?<br /> <br /> I don't mind shaking the status quo and Marvel did it many times (taking out wolverine's adamatium and healing factor - two of his defining characteristics - was a shock at the time and worked out awesome for example), but I can't understand the point of gender/race changes just for the sake of it!<br /> <br /> Marvel is no longer about comics and stories, it's money &amp; politics together hand in hand. And that really disappointed me... I know everything has to generate profit but nowadays it does at cost of imagination, depth and storytelling. It only feels cheesy, not challenging. <br /> <br /> P.S. - Props JimB you actually made a case for yourself, usually this only gets flame wars <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T08:26:46-07:00","id":262880,"title":"","content":"The back of <i>Death of Wolverine #1</i> has an interview with Wolvie's co-creator Len Wein and he actually says &quot;...let's be honest - he's not staying away. He's the most lucrative character Marvel has these days. There's no sane way a major corporation is going to decide, &quot;You know - let's knock off the guy who makes us the most money.&quot; He'll be back.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T12:31:23-07:00","id":263017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=262771#post262771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone, I think someone on this forum site, pointed out, that is a big financial risk. By making an event out of the change, Marvel attracts new readers who might get hooked and probably keeps more old readers on the current title than they lose to outrage; that built-in audience will serve as a basis for predicting whether the character's eventual ongoing book will be profitable to make. I don't know what the problem is with shaking up the status quo anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>It must be re-emphasized that it does work. I've never considered picking up a non-Alan Moore/non-Sandman Western comic before in my life, but this pitch has me wanting to subscribe for a while and see how they go about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T12:35:45-07:00","id":263021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=262835#post262835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there was any proof of anything then it would be official reason, what I wrote is what I think is really behind all these changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I just dislike people posting such theories as fact; it strikes me as somewhat dirty pool. Sorry to say that, since you've been fairly calm and nice, so I don't want to piss you off. It's just how I feel about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=262835#post262835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Samuel L. Jackson as Nick Fury? Really?!? The resemblance is uncanny!</div> </div> </div> </div>The resemblance is quite good to the Nick Fury of the Ultimate universe, but really, that's irrelevant to me. Fictional characters do not have a race, on account of being fictional. What they have is continuity. If someone had claimed the Nick Fury of the cinematic universe is intended to be exactly the same person as the Nick Fury of the 616 comics universe, then I'd say race matters, but since no one has ever made that claim, it doesn't matter. He could be a blue-skinned, no-armed hermaphroditic fungus in the movies for all it matters as long as he fills the same narrative role Nick Fury fills.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T12:39:43-07:00","id":263025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=262762#post262762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marvel completely ran out of ideas and started screwing up everything so just they can sell more comic books even if it's just for all fans to by and &quot;see how it turns out, maybe it's good&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is nothing new. The comic book industry pushed itself into this corner decades ago. The biggest profits come from balancing maintaining a stable of popular big sellers and shaking things up enough that things don't become too repetitive and stale.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the shake-ups themselves have grown repetitive and stale. Nothing Marvel is doing right now is new, unexpected, or ground-breaking.<br /> <br /> What's disturbing about the current trend is not what Marvel is doing, but the fan reactions. Marvel is doing what it has been doing for at least 30 years, but they are at least using the chance to address things like diversity in their main line up (that's supposed to be a good thing!). And the reaction to this has been to complain <i>more</i> about another shake up because Marvel is trying to do something that should be an overall positive thing along with stuff they would have done anyway (&quot;kill off&quot; a main character, pass a legacy to a different character, etc. these things happen all the time).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not the woman superhero that bothers me, but the substitution of Thor. </div> </div> </div>I think I've already addressed this very thoroughly already. This is not the first substitution of Thor. If that bothers you... well tough. That happens to Thor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's get rid of Falcon because he isn't popular enough and make him Captain American to show the world we are culturally diverse and in touch with the modern times! </div> </div> </div>Fun facts:<br /> <br /> Sam will be the 8th Captain America and the <b>2nd</b> African American one.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the core themes that the modern Captain America comics can explore is the disparity of the 40s patriotic ideal of the American Dream as embodied by the nigh flawless Steve Rogers against reality of modern life in America. The problem is that has been done to death. It's a good story, but they've done it. An African American character taking up the mantle of Captain America lets them explore this from another angle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Marvel wants more women, gays, different races, etc. build new and interesting superheroes/villains! I'm all up for that and support it 100%. But could it not mess with around with our childhood heroes? DC wanted a Batgirl they did a Batgirl, they didn't replace Batman! </div> </div> </div>Creating new characters and actually making them successful is difficult. Most new characters just become background characters to the traditional main cast. Making your main cash-cow cast diverse is not as simple as making up a bunch of new characters. Batgirl is actually an excellent example. The Batgirls have had an incredibly tough time earning a spot on the &quot;important enough to have their own regular book in perpetuity&quot; roster. They get cancelled and restarted a lot. Batman is also another character with plenty of people besides Bruce Wayne taking up the cowl.<br /> <br /> Considering that Batman, Batgirl, and Robin have all had multiple people underneath over the years... you might want to reconsider things a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I there was any proof of anything then it would be official reason, what I wrote is what I think is really behind all these changes. And you've seen it in the movies. Samuel L. Jackson as Nick Fury? Really?!? The resemblance is uncanny! </div> </div> </div>I'm taking it you're unfamiliar with the Marvel Ultimate Universe and its impact on the Marvel Cinematic Universe.<br /> <br /> The MCU takes much of its character design from the MUU, rather than the main Marvel 616 Universe, while generally taking more of their characterizations from 616. It blends the two rather thoroughly.<br /> <br /> The important thing about this is that when they started Ultimates, Marvel decided to make Nick Fury black and they went to Samuel L. Jackson specifically to use his likeness. The MUU is full of this sort of thing. Jackson said yes. And actually explicitly told them that he'd want to play Nick Fury in any movies because he loves the character. So when the MCU came around with it's blended 616 and MUU style, they honored their agreement and cast Jackson as Fury.<br /> <br /> So lets be clear. MCU Fury looks like Samuel L. Jackson because Jackson wanted to play Fury.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now the new movie of the Fantastic Four will also be featuring a black Johnny Storm / Human Torch. I can't see any reason for Marvel to be turning every damn character black! </div> </div> </div>Good thing Marvel didn't.<br /> <br /> The Fantastic Four movie rights are currently in the hands of 20th Century Fox. Marvel had no say in their decision to change Johnny.<br /> <br /> It does help to keep things things in mind. For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they want racial diversity do a movie based on Bishop, he is one of the most badass and interesting characters in the X-Men and Marvel Universe! </div> </div> </div>Fox owns the rights to the X-men franchise films. Marvel can't do a Bishop movie. And Bishop is still a regular part of the X-Men line-up in the comics.<br /> <br /> Things are way more complicated than you're giving them credit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't mind shaking the status quo and Marvel did it many times (taking out wolverine's adamatium and healing factor - two of his defining characteristics - was a shock at the time and worked out awesome for example), but I can't understand the point of gender/race changes just for the sake of it! </div> </div> </div>Why assume it is just for the sake of it?<br /> <br /> Why not assume they're doing it because they had a cool idea about a story to tell?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Marvel is no longer about comics and stories, it's money &amp; politics together hand in hand. And that really disappointed me... I know everything has to generate profit but nowadays it does at cost of imagination, depth and storytelling. It only feels cheesy, not challenging. </div> </div> </div>And yet you're actively ignoring the fact that these sorts of things <i>open up</i> the comics to do more imaginative, deep, and interesting stories. A Thor that is always Thor Odinson never changes. His stories grow stale, shallow, and boring.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T14:46:49-07:00","id":263133,"title":"","content":"Well, I remain unconvinced but I have to hand it to you guys posting some good arguments and perhaps I need to review some of my perspectives. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the discussion though, got me to search and dig deeper into the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T15:01:02-07:00","id":263148,"title":"","content":"&quot;Opening up&quot; the comics to do what a few consider to be more &quot;imaginative deep and interesting&quot; tend to be a massive failure as the characters inevitably return to form.... Thor Odinson will return just as Wolverine will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T18:07:30-07:00","id":263289,"title":"","content":"The failure rate really isn't that high if you consider that the expectation is always that things will go back to normal. There are actually a lot of pretty good little stories from stuff like this. The fact that things go back to the status quo later doesn't change that. The hold World War Hulk/Planet Hulk arc was actually pretty interesting as a story. Even if Hulk eventually came back to Earth to deal with his messed up relationships in between smashing stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T18:29:32-07:00","id":263292,"title":"","content":"*nods* World War Hulk was indeed interesting. I saw that as more of a logical progression in character that was much long delayed. &quot;Crisis on Infinite Earths&quot; was to me a big opening up moment for DC. For the longest time I had ignored DC, but that got my attention. And my money!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T02:25:57-07:00","id":264463,"title":"","content":"I know that comics always do there run, tell their stories, and then its on to another new [insert title character here] #1 and another tale... but what if after so many decades of that being true, Thor is a woman <i>and stays as such even when it's time for another THOR #1?</i><br /> <br /> Me, I am down for that.<br /> <br /> Of course, I haven't actually read comics in some years now... but this Thor is a woman now and Wolverine is dead stuff, well... that's got me thinking I'll be reading comics again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T18:21:40-07:00","id":267100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=199037#post199037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the interviews indicate Thor isn't going to be proving he's worthy again. This new woman is Thor from here on out...</div> </div> </div> </div>The interviews said Doctor Octopus posessing Spiderman's Body was the new Status Quo.<br /> <br /> These chucklefucks lie all the goddamned time about where the Status Quo's going or why it's changing, it's practically company policy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T21:32:15-07:00","id":267188,"title":"","content":"&quot;THIS IS THE NEW STATUS QUO!!!!!!!!!! Until a year or two from now when we find out no one likes what we did. Then we'll pull something out of our asses to fix it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T06:59:13-07:00","id":267384,"title":"","content":"I suppose if a person wants to be pedantic about it, there's room to argue that a state of affairs expected to last for an entire year or longer can be called a status quo. It all depends on how long a span of time you think is required for something to be a status quo.<br /> <br /> Also, when I clicked this link, it said AzraelFirestorm was the last person to post in this thread, about an hour after Papa Bear did; but I can't see any post written by him. What the what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T08:01:54-07:00","id":267410,"title":"","content":"omg...are we in the twilightzone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T08:18:03-07:00","id":267414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=267410#post267410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">omg...are we in the twilightzone?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T08:28:48-07:00","id":267430,"title":"","content":"Well there's a lack of sparkly vampires so far, so I'm thinking not...<br /> <br /> [exit stage left]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T13:15:03-07:00","id":268494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=267430#post267430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there's a lack of sparkly vampires so far, so I'm thinking not...<br /> <br /> [exit stage left]</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, I know what Odd Canuck looks like.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://media-cache-ec0.pinimg.com/736x/af/bd/20/afbd205892a2494d6d3654fc345af4fa.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T04:26:58-07:00","id":270725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=263025#post263025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is nothing new. The comic book industry pushed itself into this corner decades ago. The biggest profits come from balancing maintaining a stable of popular big sellers and shaking things up enough that things don't become too repetitive and stale.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the shake-ups themselves have grown repetitive and stale. Nothing Marvel is doing right now is new, unexpected, or ground-breaking.<br /> <br /> What's disturbing about the current trend is not what Marvel is doing, but the fan reactions. Marvel is doing what it has been doing for at least 30 years, but they are at least using the chance to address things like diversity in their main line up (that's supposed to be a good thing!). And the reaction to this has been to complain <i>more</i> about another shake up because Marvel is trying to do something that should be an overall positive thing along with stuff they would have done anyway (&quot;kill off&quot; a main character, pass a legacy to a different character, etc. these things happen all the time).<br /> <br /> Creating new characters and actually making them successful is difficult. Most new characters just become background characters to the traditional main cast. Making your main cash-cow cast diverse is not as simple as making up a bunch of new characters. Batgirl is actually an excellent example. The Batgirls have had an incredibly tough time earning a spot on the &quot;important enough to have their own regular book in perpetuity&quot; roster. They get cancelled and restarted a lot. Batman is also another character with plenty of people besides Bruce Wayne taking up the cowl.<br /> <br /> Considering that Batman, Batgirl, and Robin have all had multiple people underneath over the years... you might want to reconsider things a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look at the global comic industry as a whole, you'll notice that this problem is localised to more or less only Marvel and DC since they're the publishers that want to have their cake and eat it too. In the rest of the industry there isn't a 'traditional main cast' for the new character to become background to because the characters don't exist in a shared universe with a supposedly consistent continuity across decades of varied artists and writers. The closest you get are disney comics however those never pretend that anything that happens in comic A affects comic B, for most practical purposes each strip is its own universe.<br /> <br /> If you look at One Piece by Eiichiro Oda for instance, that comic has been going on for 17 years now with the same artist/writer all the way through, I suspect they've never even considered the idea to 'shake things up' by changing the Straw Hat pirates genders or whatever because they're actually telling a proper if very long story and once it's completed or Oda dies of old age, they won't be making One Piece Ultimate, they'll just be releasing another story by another author.<br /> <br /> I think we're also seeing more and more independent artists rebelling against the Marvel/DC model and breaking out into their own through webcomics/kickstarter with the most notable example being Girl Genius. I wouldn't be particularly surprised if in another decade or so the Marvel/DC comic divisions are completely wiped out and they're left to just making action movies while the independent comics conquer the market.<br /> <br /> What I would -love- to see is a system similar to Steam Curator for comics, where I can easily find quality comics similar to comics I already like since voter based systems that are currently common just gets you the comics that work the hardest at making people vote.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 10-02-2014, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T06:39:34-07:00","id":270786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270725#post270725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the global comic industry as a whole, you'll notice that this problem is localised to more or less only Marvel and DC since they're the publishers that want to have their cake and eat it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Marvel and DC have a lot of history. and have become the business of icons for comic-books. Add in that they are now, more or less, subsidiaries of much larger business entities, they have a lot more capital to play with, and lose since public perception is always a factor. Other publishers can only dream of what Marvel and DC accomplished over the years. The rest of the industry doesn't make a blip on public awareness. (The only exception was in the late 90s when Image first came around, and that awareness didn't last long. Today some people <i>might</i> remember Spawn, but that's pretty much it.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T07:24:00-07:00","id":270800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270786#post270786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marvel and DC have a lot of history. and have become the business of icons for comic-books. Add in that they are now, more or less, subsidiaries of much larger business entities, they have a lot more capital to play with, and lose since public perception is always a factor. Other publishers can only dream of what Marvel and DC accomplished over the years. The rest of the industry doesn't make a blip on public awareness. (The only exception was in the late 90s when Image first came around, and that awareness didn't last long. Today some people <i>might</i> remember Spawn, but that's pretty much it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'll be surprised if you look at the size of companies such as Egmont(Largest European publisher) or Shueisha (The people who publish Shonen Jump). The difference is that other publishers do not market themselves the way DC and Marvel does, if you pick up a Marvel comic it'll say &quot;MARVEL Comics&quot; in large letters on the front, if you pick up an Egmont comic it'll say &quot;Egmont publishing&quot; in small type on the third page with the copyright statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 10-02-2014, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T07:31:14-07:00","id":270804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270725#post270725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the global comic industry as a whole, you'll notice that this problem is localised to more or less only Marvel and DC since they're the publishers that want to have their cake and eat it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent. The issue, as I put it, is money.<br /> <br /> The south east Asian comics (I know I'm lumping a few fairly disparate things together there) do avoid the problems Marvel and DC have creatively, but have plenty of their own. But they're simply not as valuable as intellectual property. One Piece is a really fun manga and a really fun show. It's earned it's extremely long run and hasn't fallen for the &quot;status quo shake up trap.&quot; But when you look at the numbers... Spiderman is flat out way more profitable despite it. One could argue that in many ways Spiderman kicks Luffy's ass in profit because of it. Though there are also plenty of comics that don't managed to keep from the status quo issue that don't come from the big two. Japanese markets just usually kick in and end series to start new ones to avoid this being common.<br /> <br /> One Piece is also something of an outlier for comics from that region that manage to last that long. Bleach is still zombie trudging along and suffers plenty of the same issues as Marvel/DC status quo. The Gundam franchise could be seen in the same light (even if they're more anime focused, they do plenty of manga, and both are really vehicles to shill what makes the real money: model kits) as the repetition of plots is a bit obnoxious over time. In the long running single continuity area, the vast majority of them fall into the inevitable trap that Marvel and DC did. It's just that in many other regions there is little expectations of most comics going that long in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think we're also seeing more and more independent artists rebelling against the Marvel/DC model and breaking out into their own through webcomics/kickstarter with the most notable example being Girl Genius. I wouldn't be particularly surprised if in another decade or so the Marvel/DC comic divisions are completely wiped out and they're left to just making action movies while the independent comics conquer the market. </div> </div> </div>While I think the current status of the industry allows indie comics successes that they just couldn't get access to before, they're not killing off Marvel and DC anytime soon. They make too much money despite all their problems. Girl Genius is profitable, but she isn't pulling in a few million dollars a month in sales. There isn't going to be a massive blockbuster-fest of profits from a bunch of Girl Genius movies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T07:44:49-07:00","id":270813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270804#post270804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot; But when you look at the numbers... Spiderman is flat out way more profitable despite it. One could argue that in many ways Spiderman kicks Luffy's ass in profit because of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which numbers?<br /> <br /> Weekly Shounen Jump (Which to be fair includes Naruto, Bleach AND One Piece) has a 2.7 million circulation and as off 2013-11-21 One Piece had shipped 345 million copies of the tank\u014dbons. Over a 17 year periods the tank\u014dbon alone represent 1,7 million copies per month or 4.8 million copies of each volume.<br /> <br /> If you look at <a href=\"http://www.comichron.com/monthlycomicssales/2014/2014-08.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.comichron.com/monthlycomi...4/2014-08.html</a><br /> <br /> The entirety of the american comic book industry struggles to reach 1.7 million copies when you and them all up and Amazing Spiderman #1 which sold '<a href=\"http://blog.comichron.com/2014/05/april-2014-comics-sales-amazing-spider.html\" target=\"_blank\">amazingly</a>', Only sold a mere half a million or so. All the numbers I can find tell me One Piece is bigger then DC and Marvel put together, much less Spiderman. Profit is a lot harder to judge as those numbers are not public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T07:51:23-07:00","id":270815,"title":"","content":"I should start by pointing out I'm not into American super hero comic at all, but from my perspective, the interesting thing about this sex change will be how the character is handled during her time as Thor. Will there be perceivable differences in the subject matter or perspectives of her stories? And if they are, will they carry over to the next Thor when they change it back again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T08:23:45-07:00","id":270819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270725#post270725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at One Piece by Eiichiro Oda for instance, that comic has been going on for 17 years now with the same artist/writer all the way through, I suspect they've never even considered the idea to 'shake things up' by changing the Straw Hat pirates genders or whatever because they're actually telling a proper if very long story and once it's completed or Oda dies of old age, they won't be making One Piece Ultimate, they'll just be releasing another story by another author.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the best of examples, considering that One Piece's story isn't really interesting on the whole.<br /> <br /> Stories need an end, or they inevitably drive themselves into the ground. Or to put it another way....&quot;You either die a hero or live long enough to see yourself become the villain&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T08:48:30-07:00","id":270827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270819#post270819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the best of examples, considering that One Piece's story isn't really interesting on the whole.<br /> <br /> Stories need an end, or they inevitably drive themselves into the ground. Or to put it another way....&quot;You either die a hero or live long enough to see yourself become the villain&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now that's where you are plain wrong. Even though I don't like &quot;One Piece&quot; (mainly due to the horrible artwork) it is considered one of the best Manga and Anime series of all time. It's been praised by critics and public as one of the most compelling and well written stories. Also the fact that lasts 17 without losing popularity is a testament to it's quality. Lasts 17 years still being the hero without becoming the villain. Just because you don't like it personally doesn't make it any less good.<br /> <br /> On the other hand Marvel went through the Golden Age of Comics, Silver Age of Comics and now not only haven they been sold they are trying every and anything just to stay alive, including a woman Thor, a black Captain America and a dead Wolverine. None of that will last, it'll only generate controversy, controversy is good publicity and some hardcore fans will still buy, other will buy from curiosity and numbers increase. Next year all goes back to what it was but Marvel pocketed a couple of bucks.<br /> <br /> Despite all of this, the Thor, Captain American and Death of Wolverine MIGHT be good, but in the end it will fall short and no one will remember these times as classic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T09:00:23-07:00","id":270831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270819#post270819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the best of examples, considering that One Piece's story isn't really interesting on the whole.<br /> <br /> Stories need an end, or they inevitably drive themselves into the ground. Or to put it another way....&quot;You either die a hero or live long enough to see yourself become the villain&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike many other stories however, One Piece already had the entire story arc (including the end!) planned out from the beginning. The writer is just taking a rather long route to get there, not unlike GRRM that had originally planned 3 novels for ASOIAF and ended up with 7. Throughout the entire series Shanks and Mihawk havn't moved while Luffy and Zoro have been steadily getting closer. You can contrast that to Naruto or Bleach where the the benchmark for what counts as a badass gets raised with every new chapter or superhero comics where peoples power level can sometimes shift panel to panel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T09:17:21-07:00","id":270852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270800#post270800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you'll be surprised if you look at the size of companies such as Egmont(Largest European publisher) or Shueisha (The people who publish Shonen Jump). The difference is that other publishers do not market themselves the way DC and Marvel does, if you pick up a Marvel comic it'll say &quot;MARVEL Comics&quot; in large letters on the front, if you pick up an Egmont comic it'll say &quot;Egmont publishing&quot; in small type on the third page with the copyright statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the examples you've mentioned so far...I've never heard of before. If they are considered a &quot;success,&quot; then it's one they've carved out in some niche that doesn't come up in on the radar of the mainstream of public awareness.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T09:54:45-07:00","id":270875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270852#post270852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the examples you've mentioned so far...I've never heard of before. If they are considered a &quot;success,&quot; then it's one they've carved out in some niche that doesn't come up in on the radar of the mainstream of public awareness.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They're not niche, their revenues are measured in billions*. Egmont mostly publishes licensed comics such as Donald Duck, Tintin, Winnie the Pooh, Hello Kitty etc. They do have original comics as well but you are extremely unlikely to have heard of them if you live outside Scandinavia (Nemi, Rocky, Elvis, 87:an etc).<br /> <br /> *In Egmonts case only a fraction of that comes from comics as they have over time expanded from just publishing Donald Duck to becoming a media empire.<br /> <br /> The point here is that the fact you've heard of a publisher or not says fuck all about how succesful they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:47:12-07:00","id":270944,"title":"","content":"And how does Donald Duck comics measure up to all the publicity that even a 2nd string character Marvel comic character is receiving from a simple gender change?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T10:52:08-07:00","id":270946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270725#post270725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the global comic industry as a whole, you'll notice that this problem is localised to more or less only Marvel and DC</div> </div> </div> </div>Never heard of Tenchi Muyo, have you? They've redone Tenchi's origin story and meeting his harem like 8 different times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:09:25-07:00","id":270958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270946#post270946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never heard of Tenchi Muyo, have you? They've redone Tenchi's origin story and meeting his harem like 8 different times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it happens. However Tenchi Muyo isn't so much an example of &quot;ZOMG, it's so hard to make a new succesful character&quot; but rather more like &quot;Let's have fun with reinventing this character 8 times&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270944#post270944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how does Donald Duck comics measure up to all the publicity that even a 2nd string character Marvel comic character is receiving from a simple gender change?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By which measure? He's the only non-tabloid you are guaranteed to find in every newspaper stand in the entire country. It's hard to describe how popular he is in Sweden and certain other parts of Europe. In Scandinavia alone Donald Duck sells around 450k comics a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 10-02-2014, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T12:17:19-07:00","id":271022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=270852#post270852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the examples you've mentioned so far...I've never heard of before. If they are considered a &quot;success,&quot; then it's one they've carved out in some niche that doesn't come up in on the radar of the mainstream of public awareness.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, Donald Duck is like the <i>biggest</i> comic in Sweden. No contest even. Marvel has a healthy presence, DC less so, and One Piece is coming out regularly, but Donald Duck is what people think about when they hear &quot;comic book&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or well, when they hear &quot;serietidning&quot;, but you get what I mean.<br /> <br /> Looking at the attention Thor's gender change gets and comparing it to similar attention for Donald Duck is not really a very good way of measuring popularity. This is mainly because the two comics are very different beasts. Not only do they differ in tone, subject matter and intended audience, but there very assumption of the format is different. Donald Duck comics are not concerned with a canon, at least not in the sense that every issue progresses the story and those events will have to be taken into consideration later. Donald's canon is more of a set of basic assumptions: he has an uncle named Scrooge, he's competing for Daisy with Gladstone, and his three nephews live with him. Beyond that, few things will have permanence. I can't count all the times Donald has been scared by ghosts or been abducted by aliens, and yet when it happens the next time he's still equally surprised at their existence.<br /> <br /> If someone wanted to switch Donald into a woman, they could probably do that. It's just one more of all the strange things that happen and are promptly forgot for the next issue, or hell, the next story in the same issue. The way the authorship works (at least in the Swedish comic books), with several different authors all doing their own thing with in most cases very little collaboration, there's no way something like that would stick. Therefore, the lack of such controversy regarding Donald Duck should not be taken a sign that Donald Duck is less popular than Thor, since the circumstances make is much harder to actually effectuate said controversy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-02-2014, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T14:44:09-07:00","id":271121,"title":"","content":"A Donald Duck comic-book wouldn't mean anything here. And heaven help Disney if they even considered making him...a woman. In that, I would submit that the publicity would be incredible. But I'm almost certain it would be very negative and would likely mean lost revenue. And I mean no offense, but Sweden doesn't compare well to the US since the population is over 30x larger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T15:08:25-07:00","id":271128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=271121#post271121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Donald Duck comic-book wouldn't mean anything here. And heaven help Disney if they even considered making him...a woman. In that, I would submit that the publicity would be incredible. But I'm almost certain it would be very negative and would likely mean lost revenue. And I mean no offense, but Sweden doesn't compare well to the US since the population is over 30x larger.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you take the fact that Donald Duck sells 450k copies per week in scandinavia while Batman/Superman/Spiderman/X-Men tend to do about 50k per month each you'll realize that Donald Duck is so much more popular in Scandinavia then Batman/Spiderman is in the US that it's not even funny. (More then 10x the sales in less then 1/30th the population makes it atleast 300x more popular).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T15:59:19-07:00","id":271154,"title":"","content":"I am always pleased to see empirical math in a discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T16:49:43-07:00","id":271193,"title":"","content":"I think the interesting difference between DC/Marvel when compared to Scandinavian Donald Duck comics are how they have evolved over time. Originally DC/Marvel published pulp paper comics aimed at kids while nowadays they make glossy comics aimed at adults. Meanwhile Donald Duck is still a pulp paper comic aimed at kids which remains remarkably popular among adults since the stories are very short and entertaining which makes them very accessible. The Donald Duck publisher never feels the need to 'shake up' the Donald Duck universe because as Wiemann notes, there is no permanence in the first place, in fact they commonly republish old popular stories since the story is still good and most people will have either never read it or forgotten it.<br /> <br /> Now I bought up Donald Duck mainly to illustrate that DC/Marvel are not that dominant in the comic industry, however when it comes to introducing new characters it's a terrible example as I'm not sure if a single permanent cast member has been added in the past 50 years. It's just the kind of thing where people do seem content reading the same kind of stories about the same kind of characters in perpetuity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T19:30:27-07:00","id":271288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=271154#post271154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am always pleased to see empirical math in a discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>An &quot;If&quot; statement?<br /> <br /> How about sales instead; <a href=\"http://www.comichron.com/yearlycomicssales.html\" target=\"_blank\">Yearly Sales in North America</a><br /> <br /> In 2013;<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('di