lass=\"text_table_td1 text_table_t1_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\"> 8.70%</td> </tr> </table></div> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T20:12:59-07:00","id":271349,"title":"","content":"Shadowflame, Zironic <i>did</i> talk about sales. What you're talking about are shares of the North American market; that doesn't relate to the European market at all.<br /> <br /> But let's talk sales. If it's true as Zironic says that Donald Duck sells about 450k copies per week in Scandinavia (which, admittedly, I'd like a source on), and I compare that number to the sales of, say, Amazing Spiderman, which from the site you provided sold <a href=\"http://www.comichron.com/titlespotlights/amazingspiderman.html\" target=\"_blank\">about 116k copies during the entirety of 2008</a>, there can't really be any argument about which comic sells more. 450k sales/week by 52 weeks makes 23.4 million copies a year, about 201 times the sales. And, as Zironic pointed out, this is from a population of about <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norway\" target=\"_blank\">20</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweden\" target=\"_blank\">million</a> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denmark\" target=\"_blank\">people</a>, whereas the US has about <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States\" target=\"_blank\">319 million people</a>. If you calculate sales per capita, that comes down to... wait, 1.17 copies per capita? That's... not really reasonable, is it? I'd really like a source on those sales numbers for Donald Duck, actually.<br /> <br /> Well that kind of petered out, didn't it? I'll have to check the numbers. It's possible they're about all kinds of Donald Duck media, not just the actual comic book Donald Duck.<br /> <br /> But while I will do that, that doesn't really relate to my point, which is that talking sales is a <i>stupid thing to do</i> in this case. It's obvious that this is about two different types of popularity. Even people in Sweden will talk much more about American comics than Donald Duck, because there's nothing to discuss in Donald Duck. They just buy the stuff.<br /> <br /> The fact that one thing is popular in one way in one part of the world doesn't mean that things that are popular in other ways in other parts of the world somehow loses. There is no contest here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-02-2014, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T20:15:45-07:00","id":271350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=271288#post271288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An &quot;If&quot; statement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the conditional modifier in that statement does not apply to the numbers but rather to your specific willingness to accept them, yes. An &quot;if&quot; statement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T21:03:44-07:00","id":271365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowflame, Zironic did talk about sales. What you're talking about are shares of the North American market; that doesn't relate to the European market at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> *shrugs* North American market is the biggest in the world. The 450k figure was from an &quot;if&quot; statement. Perhaps rather than provide a link I should I have responded in kind, with an adjustment to factor in the vast difference in population size...no? But I agree with you in that there isn't a contest here. Disney is the only winner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T21:43:22-07:00","id":271370,"title":"","content":"No, the if statement didn't assume the sales figures. It said that if you accept them, you'll see how much bigger they are. There's still no source, so I'll understand if you don't, but the post didn't assume the actual numbers. That's clear from the formulation.<br /> <br /> Also, are you saying that North American comic book market is bigger than Japan's? I'd like a source on <i>that</i>, please. According to Anime News Network, the market research firm Oricon states that the <a href=\"http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2012-01-23/2011-comic-sales-totaled-271.71-billion-yen-in-japan\" target=\"_blank\">comic book market in Japan 2011</a> came in at about 503.61 million copies for a total of $3.533 billion. According to your link, <a href=\"http://www.comichron.com/yearlycomicssales.html\" target=\"_blank\">that same year, the North American market size</a> was about $715 million. Respectable, certainly, but Japan is still roughly five times larger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T23:26:45-07:00","id":271434,"title":"","content":"My source for One Piece sales:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2013-11-21/one-piece-manga-has-345-million-copies-in-print-worldwide\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news...rint-worldwide</a><br /> <br /> My source for Donald Duck sales:*<br /> <a href=\"http://www.google.se/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;ved=0CCsQFjAC&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.nordicom.gu.se%2Fsites%2Fdefault%2Ffiles%2Fmedieforskning-statistik%2F1619_2050_mags_topbycategory_2008.xls&amp;ei=3kAuVOPlIcL8aKaogMAH&amp;usg=AFQjCNHp7hMLKnQM2rag1D0GmaPdN97mOw&amp;sig2=3iRDzvTLxQxHEajLtLT2pQ&amp;bvm=bv.76802529,d.d2s&amp;cad=rja\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.google.se/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;...,d.d2s&amp;cad=rja</a><br /> <br /> My source for American comic sales:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.comichron.com/monthlycomicssales/2014/2014-08.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.comichron.com/monthlycomi...4/2014-08.html</a><br /> <br /> *Some interesting notes are that Finland by itself represent 66% of the sales even though it only represents 20% of the population and that Swedish circulation has fallen from 225k in 1990 to 132k in 2004, 83k in 2008 and 65k in 2010. If I had to guess I think they've been rapidly losing sales to people that rather browse the internet on their telephone then read funny comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 10-03-2014, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T02:17:22-07:00","id":271493,"title":"","content":"All of this is very much missing my point.<br /> <br /> The issue is not how many individual copies are sold. Print is a very low profit margin industry.<br /> <br /> My point was on the actual market value of the IP. Spiderman, not any specific Spiderman comic, is worth far more than One Piece is. That's what traps Marvel and DC in the perpetual status quo cycle. You change Spiderman too much in the comics, and you harm the total market value of the character because of the nature of how Western comics are done. Donald's success in Europe reinforces my point.<br /> <br /> The Manga industry his more open to getting away from this cycle in a few ways. One of which is that the industry is a mix of either driven by merchandise that needs constant changes in the source material (ex: Gundam) or largely doesn't drive multimedia empires beyond telling the story (ex: One Piece). When One Piece ends, it ends. The structure of the part of the industry then uses its success to push new projects from the publisher and the creative teams. But this invariably means no single property is actually worth that much in total because the expectation is always that it is limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T02:42:50-07:00","id":271497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=271493#post271493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this is very much missing my point.<br /> <br /> The issue is not how many individual copies are sold. Print is a very low profit margin industry.<br /> <br /> My point was on the actual market value of the IP. Spiderman, not any specific Spiderman comic, is worth far more than One Piece is. That's what traps Marvel and DC in the perpetual status quo cycle. You change Spiderman too much in the comics, and you harm the total market value of the character because of the nature of how Western comics are done. Donald's success in Europe reinforces my point.<br /> <br /> The Manga industry his more open to getting away from this cycle in a few ways. One of which is that the industry is a mix of either driven by merchandise that needs constant changes in the source material (ex: Gundam) or largely doesn't drive multimedia empires beyond telling the story (ex: One Piece). When One Piece ends, it ends. The structure of the part of the industry then uses its success to push new projects from the publisher and the creative teams. But this invariably means no single property is actually worth that much in total because the expectation is always that it is limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we disagree. Originally before I got sidetracked by digging up sales data I was trying to argue that the inability to create new characters instead of just rehashing the old ones is not an inherent property of comics. I also don't think 'shaking things up' every few years for extra publicity is neccesary either. I think they're both symptoms of the fact that Marvel and DC for a few decades now have been 'brand' companies rather then comic companies. My suspicion is that when DC/Marvel 'shake things up' for publicity, they don't do it to increase comic sales as they are rather abyssmal either way, but rather by constantly pushing their brands into newspaper articles they keep their trademarks relevant and let them earn money from their real profit center, licensing and merchandise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T07:51:24-07:00","id":271620,"title":"","content":"The problem is that Marvel and DC get the attention because of the size of their brands. But a lot of comic book companies are brand based in their market value.<br /> <br /> In Europe, comics are mostly a brand based market. The companies in question that are generally putting out way more than comics. Does Scandinavia love the hell out of Donald Duck? Yes, but he's a brand.<br /> <br /> The south east Asian comic market avoids being so dominated by this, but it still sets in. When branding is the major driver of an IP, it is generally very consciously done to drive a consumer desire for new stuff. A lot of things are just long comic/animated commercials for something more lucrative, and regularly changing things gives you more of that lucrative new things to sell. The stories in such properties tend to fall into the same repetitive status quo issues as Western comics. Even when you look at the bigger comic-as-primary-value driven manga, it is exceedingly rare for them to reach the kind of sizes that we associate with the &quot;big names&quot; of manga stories. And most of them get there by similar storytelling tactics. The shonen genre is notoriously prone to this. Sure we have One Piece (though even it isn't actually immune from, &quot;New Island with [dangerous mystery], Luffy idiot heroes his way through the situation while the others put up with it and do their best to help; if [big bad is behind the mystery] the Strawhats will have a major setback before getting stronger and winning.&quot; but you also have Bleach, Naruto, Dragonball, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T08:01:32-07:00","id":271624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=271620#post271620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And most of them get there by similar storytelling tactics. The shonen genre is notoriously prone to this. Sure we have One Piece (though even it isn't actually immune from, &quot;New Island with [dangerous mystery], Luffy idiot heroes his way through the situation while the others put up with it and do their best to help; if [big bad is behind the mystery] the Strawhats will have a major setback before getting stronger and winning.&quot; but you also have Bleach, Naruto, Dragonball, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was part of what I was getting at, for the record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-03-2014, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T08:13:53-07:00","id":272942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=271620#post271620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And most of them get there by similar storytelling tactics. The shonen genre is notoriously prone to this. Sure we have One Piece (though even it isn't actually immune from, &quot;New Island with [dangerous mystery], Luffy idiot heroes his way through the situation while the others put up with it and do their best to help; if [big bad is behind the mystery] the Strawhats will have a major setback before getting stronger and winning.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worthwhile to point out that this storytelling tactic is just the standard 3 act play.<br /> Act 1: Setup<br /> Act 2: Setback<br /> Act 3: Victory<br /> <br /> The difference between various comics tends to be the lengths of the acts. In a Donald Duck comic each act might be 2-3 pages long while in a Manga it might be between 1-10 chapters depending on pacing. If you abandon this structure many people will feel like nothing meaningful ever happens or that everything just happens randomly. However the fact that the comic keeps repeating 3-act Arcs does not necessarily mean it is preserving status quo. A good example of this would be the korean webcomic Tower of God that's broken into very clear acts with clear developments between each act.<br /> <br /> I agree that the shonen genre in particular though does strongly favor the status quo, however I think that's forgivable since the genre is centred on fun rather then depth. If you kill off major characters every few chapters it quickly becomes much less casual reading. In series aimed at older readers such as Gantz, Elfen Lied, Kingdom, Zetman etc there are much more permanent consequences in the subplots. They're also much smaller brands which is probably related.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:51:22-07:00","id":272998,"title":"","content":"So, uh...did anyone actually read the book? I didn't buy it myself, but a friend let me bum it, and I found it pretty interesting. Starts off as a mystery and ends with one (&quot;Why isn't Mjolnir letting anyone pick it up? Who is the silhouette who approaches Mjolnir, whispers about how there must always be a Thor, and picks it up? Kind of convenient timing, isn't it? Did she have something to do with Mjolnir failing?&quot;) that I want to pick up and get into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:12:30-07:00","id":273026,"title":"","content":"I didn't realize it was out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:20:30-07:00","id":273032,"title":"","content":"Yep, hit the shelves Wednesday. I didn't notice it myself when I went to the shop, but to be honest, I likely wouldn't have picked it up on my own even if I had; I'm just not that invested in the Thor mythology. The first issue interests me, though. Strong characterization, clear stakes, clean art...I admit I skimmed through the middle bit with the dark elves just because I was among company and I didn't want to spend a lot of time reading comics in front of everyone, but the start and the end are both pretty sweet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T11:31:39-07:00","id":273099,"title":"","content":"And now I've subscribed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T13:14:47-07:00","id":273180,"title":"","content":"So not having read any other Thor comics, my main thoughts are<br /> A) Asgardia is bloody stupid<br /> B) Odin is a lot sillier then I would expect<br /> C) Skottie Youngs variant cover makes me smile<br /> D) The letter/answer section in the back appears to imply that Thor is still the main character while the female hammer holder is basically going to be Beta Ray Bill<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> According to this interview:<br /> <a href=\"http://blogs.wsj.com/speakeasy/2014/09/29/marvel-writer-jason-aaron-on-why-he-made-thor-a-woman/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blogs.wsj.com/speakeasy/2014/...-thor-a-woman/</a><br /> The intent is that she'll keep the hammer for atleast a year or two. I wouldn't be surprised if the actual length will depend on sales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 10-05-2014, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T16:02:56-07:00","id":274233,"title":"","content":"On Donald Duck and continuity:<br /> <br /> 1. Don Rosa. Most famous for \u201cThe Life and Times of Scrooge McDuck\u201d; but all of his stories invariably include references to earlier stories, even if only such things as having the group walking past a case featuring a 1916 quarter with a for sale sign it. <br /> <br /> 2. Uncle Scrooge comics and Duck Tales are essentially alternate realities in much the same way that mainstream Marvel and Ultimate Marvel are. <br /> <br /> 3. Paperinik.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T01:51:26-07:00","id":274573,"title":"","content":"1) Don Rosa doesn't get enough credit<br /> 2) Scrooge/Duck Tales stuff have a tendency to show up randomly. For instancehis secretary Miss Quackfaster and butler (Battista in italian, Albert in swedish) when the writer feels like it while sometimes the newphews are hardcore scouts and sometimes they're just normal kids. Part of the reason is that the comics are written by entirely different companies. The earliest ones were written by <i>Walt Disney's Comics and Stories </i>however they stopped producing them in 1984. Some of them are written by Scandinavian Egmont, some of them are written by Disney Italia (Who among other things invented Paperinik, Battista and Qu-Qu 7*) while some come from Netherlands/France/Germany.<br /> 3) Fun fact, he's called Steel-Donald in the Swedish version, yes his secret and real identity have the same name.<br /> <br /> *Qu-Qu 7 is his secret agent identity where he does missions for Scrooge James Bond style.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T15:04:38-07:00","id":276680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=273180#post273180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So not having read any other Thor comics, my main thoughts are<br /> A) Asgardia is bloody stupid<br /> B) Odin is a lot sillier then I would expect<br /> C) Skottie Youngs variant cover makes me smile<br /> D) The letter/answer section in the back appears to imply that Thor is still the main character while the female hammer holder is basically going to be Beta Ray Bill<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> According to this interview:<br /> <a href=\"http://blogs.wsj.com/speakeasy/2014/09/29/marvel-writer-jason-aaron-on-why-he-made-thor-a-woman/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blogs.wsj.com/speakeasy/2014/...-thor-a-woman/</a><br /> The intent is that she'll keep the hammer for atleast a year or two. I wouldn't be surprised if the actual length will depend on sales.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like She Thor is going to be our new Thunderstrike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T03:44:54-08:00","id":308021,"title":"","content":"While the idea of female Thor seems peculiar, I really should not judge given I have a genderbent Mordred in my set. Enough said, YAMATO spreading their 'Rule 63' outside Japan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T07:22:15-07:00","id":467349,"title":"","content":"Just bumping to say I'm still picking up and enjoying this book. The controversy has worn off enough that I can do so quietly without feeling like I need to defend anything and just let the story being told be what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:00:57-07:00","id":467437,"title":"","content":"My biggest problem with it remains that it plays out much like most Marvel/DC comics do, and I just don't have a taste for the tropes and style. I'm enjoying it, but I don't think I'm gonna follow it after the end of the subscription period.<br /> <br /> That said, it has prompted me to try Hellblazer once I get the money. But that's playing safe with Alan Moore again, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:50:35-07:00","id":467535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=467349#post467349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just bumping to say I'm still picking up and enjoying this book. The controversy has worn off enough that I can do so quietly without feeling like I need to defend anything and just let the story being told be what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with the character isn't that she's thor it's that it's a fairly boring soap box of a character who gets everything handed to her rather than showing something real. They could have ignored the complaints and just gone for an actual story. They went for a soap box critiquing the detractors. If you honestly believe in what you are writing the goal isn't to stoop low it's to make a good book. This is why Ms.Marvel has been a much better comic. Despite the complaints some people have about it and it does have a few flaws that get blown out of proportion. It's managed to stay a story first and for most. When kamala does weird things it's keeps with the flow of the nariative rather than oppose it or reminding me of the controversy. In general, thor just hasn't been a good book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:08:59-07:00","id":467624,"title":"","content":"I'm just not a fan of Thor. Or Marvel. I find 'Selina Kyle is now a crime boss,' more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:28:39-07:00","id":467668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/198991-thor-is-now-a-woman?p=467535#post467535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They went for a soap box critiquing the detractors.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they didn't. I've been through this elsewhere, and I went through each issue page by page and panel by panel. The soap box people insist is there just isn't. Even the people trying to kill her don't seem to care she's female.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:37:48-07:00","id":467681,"title":"","content":"Long time Thor fan here, and I'm actually surprised by all the vitriol surrounding this. It's not like characters (Loki) have been gender-swapped before!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T11:46:09-07:00","id":467690,"title":"","content":"I think TextsFromSuperheroes summed it up well:<br /> <br /> &quot;Father, I'm a woman.&quot;<br /> &quot;So has your sister-brother Loki been, and then gave birth to my horse.&quot;<br /> &quot;That reminds me, it's grandhorse's birthday soon, get him/her/it a card.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're iconic archetypes......gender starts to go out the window after a fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:11:23-07:00","id":467722,"title":"","content":"Loki-as-Woman was fantastic. I may not be a fan but I came very close to becoming a loyal one during the meat of the Broxton period. The Bill and Kelda story, especially, though I thought they sort of wrote Kelda weakly at the end.<br /> <br /> But just to clarify, it isn't Thor-as-Woman. It's another woman who gained the power of Thor, like Mjolnir promises. Even that way, however, it's hardly a new concept in comics. When Superman died, many took his place, just like when Batman 'died' and we had Dickbats for a while. More notoriously, just a few years ago Tony Stark had Thor cloned, by a Nazi no less, to replace him after his death.<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of different complaints within the people who don't like it. Some just don't think there should be a female Thor, or that she has the 'right' to call herself Thor or whatever. While others seem more concerned about the writing, like below<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://s21.postimg.org/wrbkm8d4n/1423674769863.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And they call that soap boxing and part of a double-standard, as if you turn the situation around you get something like this.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/01e240f893a88c7ce6e1b6058f1f2fef/tumblr_nk3bh6Jfdu1s5bhbfo1_1280.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I haven't been part of a debate class in eons and even when I was I didn't pay attention, but I'm sure the second picture could be dismissed as a strawman or some other flawed form of argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Just cleaning up something. I swear I've somehow gained the New Page persistent condition. 04-03-2015, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:30:11-07:00","id":468081,"title":"","content":"Yes, abusive behavior by female characters on male characters is a cliched double standard. But it is extremely pervasive, and I think the criticism misses the mark drastically here:<br /> <br /> Thor still smacks Titania. Thor, the protagonist, is the character who's morals we're supposed to by sympathetic to; not the antagonist. Thor's response to the double standard is to say, &quot;screw your double standard, that's dumb, and I'm going to hit you now.&quot; Thor's position is not, &quot;I'm female, so yay girl power and lets ignore you're the bad guy.&quot; It's, &quot;My gender is irrelevant and you're the bad guy, bringing up that we have biological parts in common isn't going to stop me from beating you up for being a bad person.&quot;<br /> <br /> The soapbox doesn't really exist if the point of that page is the hero flat out ignoring the double standard the villain tries to invoke. The gender flopped example doesn't really demonstrate anything besides, well, that Thor beats up bad people despite gender, and doesn't give a crap about stupid social norms that create sexist biases. In both the heroic action is to beat on the villain that just tried to use spousal abuse, and gender identity to get out of being beaten up for being a villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}